; AcuVoice engine configuration.
;
; avcore.dll opens this file by bare name through GetPrivateProfileString, so Windows
; resolves it against the Windows directory: this is the only place the engine will ever
; look for its directories. The installer fills the values in below.
;
; PAUSE1..PAUSE4 are lengths of silence in milliseconds -- after a sentence, at a
; semicolon or colon, at a comma, and between words. They are the only prosody the
; engine core applies itself; rate, pitch and volume are applied by the SAPI5 wrapper.
; set_pausation writes changes back here, which is why the installer gives this file an
; ACL that lets the logged-on user write to it.

[AcuVoiceAppDir]
SNDBANK=
TEMPDIR=
DICTFLSDIR=
USERDICTDIR=

[AcuVoiceSettings]
PAUSE1=650
PAUSE2=500
PAUSE3=350
PAUSE4=7

[AcuVoiceDictionary]
CUSTOM=NO
